16
00:00:56.479 --> 00:01:02.231
NARRATOR: Understanding tokenization reveals
how compilers manage language syntax before

17
00:01:02.231 --> 00:01:02.806
attempting,

18
00:01:02.954 --> 00:01:08.992
NARRATOR: Once tokens are isolated, the parser
applies language grammar and operator

19
00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:14.526
precedence to construct an abstract syntax
tree whose nodes represent expressions,

20
00:01:14.526 --> 00:01:16.539
function prototypes, and definitions.

21
00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:21.937
NARRATOR: The parser consumes the token stream
and validates syntactic structure against

22
00:01:21.937 --> 00:01:23.286
formal grammar rules.

23
00:01:23.286 --> 00:01:28.249
NARRATOR: For example, it checks that an
identifier is followed by a valid operator or

24
00:01:28.249 --> 00:01:28.911
